I like that there are options regarding dragon scale mail in Sporkhack
but I have not found much reason to not stick with silver or grey.  I
still need reflection and magic resistance and my big limitation is
that I prefer to wear an amulet of life saving since things can get
bad really fast on the Astral Plane (especially given the hp limit and
a limit on the number of full healing potions I can carry).  Therefore
reflection is either a shield or SDSM (I don't use the reflection
spell since I don't like to rely on temporary measures).  If I'm
twoweaponing or wielding a two hander then that leaves me with SDSM,
and if I'm a spellcaster then I probably don't want to use the shield
either leaving me with SDSM.  (In the case of knights and rangers I
don't like to rely on the quest artifacts for reflection given the
ability of the Wizard to steal them)  Then I also need MR and I don't
like to rely on my own quest artifact for MR so that leaves a cloak or
a cross-class quest artifact and so most often I find myself wearing a
cloak of magic resistance.  I suppose when I do have a cross-class
quest artifact then I'll use a different color DSM but some do have
some drawbacks/weaknesses.  I do _not_ rely on Magicbane as my
permanent source of MR.

I like yellow DSM for the protection from Nazgul and archons but that
prevents me from easily confusing myself for portal detection.  I do
keep a set of scales in my bag though for the nasty Nazgul.
I also like white DSM but rarely use it because I don't like having to
change out my armor for potion diluting (i.e. I'm too lazy).
Blue is probably my most common (after Silver or Grey) because then I
can wear jumping boots and still be 'very fast'.
Green is clever against minotaurs and other big creatures especially
now that many of the big creatures have so many hp now.
The benefit from red seems pretty minor as compared to the damage the
hero can dish out.  I'd probably like it better if it was a passive
fire attack, and especially if it would boil away enemies' healing
potions etc.
Black is fun for evasion and I suppose orange would be also.

